00:36:22,900 --> 00:36:23,560
Thank you.

397
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:42,200
Hello, I'm Zhebing Yang from Peking University and today I'd like to introduce our work EGO VLA.

398
00:36:42,540 --> 00:36:45,300
This work studies where should VLA models be deployed.

399
00:36:45,480 --> 00:36:49,320
The first trait is a high -end GPU such as RTX 1590,

400
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:55,980
but it will face long network latency when worked as a cloud server and high power consumption when deployed on the robots.

401
00:36:56,700 --> 00:37:00,830
Another trait is the onboard devices such as JSON -ORI or JSON -SOAR.

402
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:06,640
However, this device has limited resources, and it will introduce long inference time.

403
00:37:08,080 --> 00:37:13,300
So the question is, can we run VLA at 50 volts without affecting robot performance?

404
00:37:13,620 --> 00:37:19,560
Based on this, we propose EGO VLA, a method for efficient VLA deployment for onboard devices.

405
00:37:20,300 --> 00:37:24,800
Let me first ask how onboard long inference latency affects robot performance.

406
00:37:25,220 --> 00:37:28,130
The first challenge is prediction execution misalignment.

407
00:37:28,180 --> 00:37:32,800
As by the time actions are predicted, the worst has already changed.

408
00:37:33,700 --> 00:37:38,080
And longer latency leads to larger misalignment and SR reduction.

409
00:37:38,860 --> 00:37:44,040
So a method that predicts future information at the inference end time is needed.

410
00:37:45,760 --> 00:37:48,540
And the next challenge is the long reaction time.

411
00:37:48,860 --> 00:37:55,760
As shown in this image, robot's reaction time is strictly bounded by the inference latency delta,

412
00:37:56,180 --> 00:37:59,900
and the longer latency leads to longer reaction and SR reduction.

413
00:38:00,500 --> 00:38:04,320
So a method that accelerates action prediction is needed.

