01:00:15,460 --> 01:00:16,750
Hi, I'm Zhiyu Zhu.

630
01:00:16,800 --> 01:00:21,660
So today I'll present more mixture of experts for multi -physics robotic word models.

631
01:00:22,480 --> 01:00:24,850
So a word model can help robots in three ways.

632
01:00:24,900 --> 01:00:28,610
First, for planning, we score candidate actions and then pick the best one.

633
01:00:28,660 --> 01:00:32,090
And second, it can act as a learning simulator for I.O.

634
01:00:32,140 --> 01:00:35,920
And third, it powers imagine and act policies like WAMS.

635
01:00:36,800 --> 01:00:42,200
But existing models for short, video models predict 2D pixels and are hard to act on.

636
01:00:42,360 --> 01:00:46,180
Inverse physics models need long observation and slow system ID.

637
01:00:46,580 --> 01:00:50,700
And most 3D dynamics models here only handle one material.

638
01:00:51,080 --> 01:00:58,880
And we built on this line trying to build a single 3D world model across different materials and different actuators.

639
01:01:01,160 --> 01:01:06,840
And our key insight here is that robot interactions can form distinct dynamic groups.

640
01:01:07,080 --> 01:01:09,150
So one shared model tends to put them together.

641
01:01:09,200 --> 01:01:17,320
That is why we use a mixture of experts structure here to help us decode the latent feature into different outputs.

642
01:01:17,760 --> 01:01:20,080
And here, this is our MPC pipeline.

643
01:01:20,240 --> 01:01:24,370
We first infer the physics property here and then use MPC roll out.

644
01:01:24,420 --> 01:01:30,280
Our experiment used data from simulation, real world from PG &E paper and dry data set.

645
01:01:33,520 --> 01:01:41,620
And for the precision error, as you can see here, our method can outperform other methods.

646
01:01:41,800 --> 01:01:49,660
And here is the prediction results from the simulation and the rainbow flow here is the prediction flow of the points.

647
01:01:50,360 --> 01:01:51,690
And here is the real robot.

648
01:01:51,740 --> 01:01:55,380
But as you can see here, our model can predict the different materials.

649
01:01:56,220 --> 01:01:59,230
And the blue point here is the flow of the points.

650
01:01:59,280 --> 01:02:01,460
And the red point here is the gripper flows.

651
01:02:10,050 --> 01:02:16,690
And for the dry dataset, our prediction shows at the bottom, stay close to the ground, choose point cloud at the top.

652
01:02:24,090 --> 01:02:27,440
Now for control side, the shaded object marks the goal.

653
01:02:27,490 --> 01:02:30,360
And the more pushes the rigid objects right to it.

654
01:02:30,410 --> 01:02:34,020
And it works for the soft objects, too, as you can see in the second row.

655
01:02:34,070 --> 01:02:36,450
Like this cap and the sheep toy.

656
01:02:50,360 --> 01:02:52,540
And here is the results on the real robot.

657
01:02:52,760 --> 01:02:57,280
Our system can push a box, grasp a slot and do a multi -step task.

658
01:02:57,640 --> 01:03:01,340
Where you reach is a tissue box here with a tool and then wipes the table.

659
01:03:01,660 --> 01:03:04,480
So one more model and for many physics.

660
